     "result_text_tail": "ated because the 2028 revenue recurs.\n- **Engineering cost:** the $0.9M OEM team is counted for all three years, and 2027 uses the partner's 5,000-robot forecast. I flag that this assumes certification arrives on time.\n\n**What the second reviewer changed:** I had a second reviewer attack the recommendation before building the slides. It confirmed the arithmetic and changed three things:\n- **Volume gate:** raised from the OEM's 5,000 robots a year to about 8,800. That is what it takes to cover the team plus 70% of the lost direct profit.\n- **Liquidity claim:** narrowed to \"fundable without the advance\", because the pack gives no operating burn.\n- **New page:** I added a slide that tests \"take Option X for the cash\" on the same numbers.\n\n**QA:** the checker passes with no failures. Three warnings remain because the pack writes \"three years\", \"five competitors\" and the 100% ceiling in words, so there is no figure to match. Re-checking web sources didn't apply, since all sources are the pack. The backup table and two calculation cards show $ thousands so that values like $0.45M don't round to \"$0.5M\".\n\nThe OEM has not agreed to any of the protections, and won't guarantee the $350 price beyond the pilot. The deck says this where it matters.\n\nNext, I can switch the theme, or make a shorter board-pack version.\n\nFiles are in `deliverable/`:\n- boreal-oem-exclusivity.pptx\n- boreal-oem-exclusivity-sources.xlsx\n- boreal-oem-exclusivity.json (the spec; `work/build_spec.py` regenerates it)"
